# AI integration

- Local-first: text generation runs against a local model via Ollama.
  Don't introduce a cloud LLM API call without being explicitly asked —
  this includes convenience fallbacks "in case the local model is slow".
- Staff-authored content (an assistant coach's tactical suggestion, a
  scout's report, a fitness assessment) must have its quality/usefulness
  gated by that staff member's in-game skill attribute. A low-rated staff
  member's output should be visibly vaguer or less reliable than a
  top-rated one's — don't generate uniform-quality output regardless of
  the underlying attribute.
- Press conferences, agent/player dialogue, and similar generated content
  are not purely cosmetic — they can subtly affect morale/relationships.
  When adding a new generated-content type, consider whether it should
  feed back into morale/relationship state, not just render as flavor
  text.
- **No generative image AI** for shipped game assets (PRD 01). Use SVG, CSS,
  typography, emoji/glyphs, charts, or declared CC0 sources. If the user
  asks to generate art, refuse and point to PRD 01 — do not call image
  models or suggest Midjourney/SD pipelines.
- Optional later: developer-recorded modular voice lines (not TTS). CC0 SFX
  for matchday atmosphere is fine with attribution.
